    "text": {
     "en": "(additional, not in the textbook) Every solid has faces, edges and corners.\nA face is a flat or curved surface. An edge is where two faces meet. A corner, or vertex, is where edges meet.\nA cube has 6 faces, 12 edges and 8 corners. A cuboid also has 6 faces, 12 edges and 8 corners.\nA cylinder has 2 flat faces, 1 curved face and 2 curved edges.\nA cone has 1 flat face, 1 curved face and 1 corner at the tip."
    }
